  "preregistration": "P-AXES, frozen 2026-10-30T00:50:31Z. Axis B (work when only k of N artifacts are read per burst): the view pays its full maintenance cost per burst regardless of k (refresh_plus_publish per burst on record: ~4-7 ms collegemsg, 64-266 ms synth at 10^3, 5.35 s at 10^4). TGMS with on-demand refresh pays, per burst, k x (one check, plus one refresh when the check says possibly stale). Measure TGMS's on-demand cost per read artifact (a harness mode that refreshes only the artifacts read, k drawn uniformly per burst) at k in {1, 10, 100, N} for N = 10^3 (both stores) and k in {1, 10, 100, 1,000, N} for the probe, and compute the crossover k* where TGMS's per-burst cost equals the view's. Prediction: k* in [3, 30] at N = 10^3 on synth, k* in [100, 1,000] at N = 10^4, and <= 3 on collegemsg (the view's per-burst cost there is only ~5 ms). Falsifier: k* < 1 on synth at either N -> TGMS loses even when a single artifact is read, and the paper says the view dominates on cost in every regime.",
